# --- ZMR / ZMS miniature series -------------------------------------------
# Transcribed 2026-09-18 from printed catalog pages 55 (ZMS) and 56-58
# (ZMR), the same rendered-page-image method as the main table above.
# These are the tables the main Rectangular Boxes pages point to with
# "See page 55/56/57/58" for anything too small to carry its own inline
# gauge/radii -- a genuinely different schema from the main series:
#
# - max_depth_in: the catalog gives only ONE depth per size (no min/max
#   range), so there's no adjustable height slider for these -- height is
#   fixed at the printed value.
# - material_code: "A", "B", or "C", resolving to a different actual
#   gauge depending on which material it's drawn in -- see
#   mini_series_pricing.MATERIAL_THICKNESS_CODE for the A/B/C -> gauge
#   table and mini_series_pricing.MATERIALS for the sourced pricing of
#   each material (steel/aluminum/brass/Monel).
# - gauge_override_in: set (and material_code is None) for the few rows
#   the catalog flags "Special Gauge" with a literal thickness instead of
#   a code. Alloy density/price still comes from whichever material the
#   user picks; only the thickness is fixed. Two other rows carry
#   footnotes restricting them to a subset of materials, not enforced
#   here, and one (ZMR-094-112) lists an ambiguous "A/B" code, treated
#   as "A" -- see mini_series_pricing.py's docstring for all three.
# - r1_in/r2_in: usually one combined radius (applied to both), but five
#   rows publish two distinct values and are transcribed as such.

